/**
 * @file Logger.dox
 * @author Alexandru ALEXANDRESCU
 * @brief Doxygen documentation for the Utils::Logger module
 * 
 * @page LoggerDoxPage Logging Utility
 * @brief Logging utility with runtime API and compile-time macros.
 * 
 * ## Overview
 * The Logger module provides:
 * - Thread-safe runtime logging
 * - File rotation
 * - Optional console output
 * - Millisecond timestamps
 * - Compile-time macros for zero-cost logging in performance-critical paths
 * 
 * ## Usage
 * 
 * ### 1. Setup (Required before logging)
 * Call once at application startup:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * Utils::Logger::init("app_name", "/var/log/");
 * Utils::Logger::setLevel(Utils::LogLevel::Debug);
 * Utils::Logger::instance().setMaxSize(1024 * 1024);
 * Utils::Logger::enableConsole(true);
 * Utils::Logger::enableMilliseconds(true);
 * @endcode
 * 
 * ### 2. Runtime logging API (Less efficient, flexible)
 * Use this in normal code paths:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * Utils::Logger::info("Application started");
 * Utils::Logger::debug("Value x = 42");
 * Utils::Logger::warn("This is a warning");
 * Utils::Logger::error("Something failed");
 * @endcode
 * 
 * ### 3. Compile-time macros (Efficient, filtered by LOG_COMPILED_LEVEL)
 * These macros are compiled out if the log level is above the compiled level:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * LOG_INFO("Application started");
 * LOG_DEBUG("Value x = 42");
 * LOG_WARN("This is a warning");
 * LOG_ERROR("Something failed");
 * @endcode
 * 
 * ## Log Levels
 * | Level | Numeric Value | Macro         |
 * |-------|---------------|---------------|
 * | Trace | 0             | LOG_TRACE     |
 * | Debug | 1             | LOG_DEBUG     |
 * | Info  | 2             | LOG_INFO      |
 * | Warn  | 3             | LOG_WARN      |
 * | Error | 4             | LOG_ERROR     |
 * | Fatal | 5             | LOG_FATAL     |
 * 
 * `LOG_COMPILED_LEVEL` controls which macros are included at compile time.
 * 
 * ## Class Reference
 * ### Utils::Logger
 * Thread-safe singleton logger.
 * 
 * #### Public Methods
 * - `static Logger& instance()`  
 *   Returns the singleton instance of Logger.
 * 
 * - `static void init(std::string baseName, std::string basePath="")`  
 *   Initialize the logger. Must be called before `instance()` is accessed.
 * 
 * - `static void enableConsole(bool enable)`  
 *   Enable or disable console output.
 * 
 * - `static void enableMilliseconds(bool enable)`  
 *   Enable or disable milliseconds in timestamps.
 * 
 * - `static void setLevel(LogLevel level)`  
 *   Set runtime log level.
 * 
 * - `static void log(LogLevel level, const std::string& msg)`  
 *   Log a message at the specified level.
 * 
 * - `void setMaxSize(std::size_t s)`  
 *   Set the maximum size of log files before rotation.
 * 
 * - `std::size_t getMaxSize() const`  
 *   Returns the maximum log file size.
 * 
 * - `const std::string& getName()`  
 *   Returns the base log file name.
 * 
 * - `const std::string& getPath()`  
 *   Returns the base path for log files.
 * 
 * - Convenience methods: `info()`, `warn()`, `error()`, `debug()`  
 *   Shortcut runtime log methods.
 * 
 * #### Private Methods
 * - `logImpl(LogLevel level, const std::string& msg)`  
 *   Internal thread-safe log implementation.
 * 
 * - `openFile()`  
 *   Open the log file.
 * 
 * - `rotateFile(std::size_t incoming)`  
 *   Rotate log files if the max size is exceeded.
 * 
 * - `currentSize() const`  
 *   Returns current log file size.
 * 
 * - `makeTimestamp() const`  
 *   Return timestamp string with optional milliseconds.
 * 
 * - `static const char* toString(LogLevel level)`  
 *   Converts log level to string representation.
 * 
 * @section References
 * 
 * See @ref LoggerPage "Logger"
 *
 * See @ref LoggerConfigPage "Logger Configuration"
 * 
 */